Orchestrates three expansion passes over a parsed steno dictionary to emit `TypedEntry` records for rendering: Pass A resolves counts (repetitions and computed expressions), Pass B appends type strokes and fills type slots, and a line-flag pass sets the `one_liner` field. Consumes `@type` entries as the type-append pool and filters them from output.

Entry point is `expand_dict(entries, generic_arg_strokes)`, which returns `Vec<TypedEntry>` or `ExpandError`. It builds a type set from all entries, optionally restricts the arity-0 generic argument pool by stroke name, then iterates non-type entries through `expand_counts` (Pass A) and `expand_types_one` (Pass B), calls `fix_family_terminals` to mark terminal vs. non-terminal steps based on family relationships, and finally `expand_line_flag` to compute the `one_liner` boolean. Each `TypedEntry` carries the fully resolved stroke key, template with type slots filled, terminal/one-liner flags, count value, and a type_label when a `%t` slot was resolved.

The `ExpandedEntry` struct (Pass A output) differs from `TypedEntry` only in lacking `terminal` and `one_liner` fields — it is not persisted or exposed publicly. `generic_arg_strokes` parameter is a restriction filter; omitting it uses the full arity-0 pool. Non-fatal misconfiguration surfaces as `ExpandError` early, before any entry is partially processed.